  "code": "Anti CCP",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table><thead><tr><th><div>Anti-CCP Antibody Test Results</div></th><th><div>Interpretation</div></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><div>Positive</div></td><td><div>Indicates the presence of anti-CCP antibodies, which is strongly associated with rheumatoid arthritis (RA). Higher levels of antibodies increase the likelihood of RA.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Negative</div></td><td><div>Does not necessarily rule out RA, as some people with RA may not have detectable levels of anti-CCP antibodies. However, a negative result makes the diagnosis of RA less likely.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Interpretation</div></td><td><div>The results should be considered in conjunction with other clinical and laboratory findings to arrive at a definitive diagnosis of RA. Consult with a healthcare provider to discuss the results and their implications for overall health.</div></td></tr></tbody></table>",
